# Rule-file injection allowlist
#
# HIDDEN findings always fail and cannot be listed here: zero-width
# characters, bidi controls, HTML comments with imperative or install
# wording, invisible HTML/CSS, and lines over 400 characters.
#
# INSTRUCTION and UNKNOWN_PKG fail unless one line matches all four fields.
# Tab-separated:
#
#   path    rule    pattern    reason
#
# path     Repo-relative path, "*" for any scanned file, or an fnmatch pattern.
# rule     INSTRUCTION or UNKNOWN_PKG.
# pattern  Python regex searched against the finding text. Required.
# reason   Why this mention is legitimate. Required.
#
# This pack has no install directives in scanned rule files, so there are
# no active entries. Example, kept commented:
# skills/example/SKILL.md	INSTRUCTION	install-directive	test runner named in that skill
